# Code style

- Boring, readable code. Small files (< 200 lines), small functions (< 30 lines), one job each.
- Plain descriptive names (`split_text_into_chunks`, not `proc`).
- Comment **why**, not what, for non-obvious decisions.
- Python: ruff, type hints on every function, no `Any` unless commented. Early returns.
- TypeScript: `strict: true`, no `any`, no default exports except Next.js pages.
- Config only in `config.py` / env. No scattered `os.environ`.
- Every external call has a timeout and bounded retry (max 3).
